# Project Overview

This is a Clash of Clans farming bot running on Python 3.11.

# Bot Runtime Flow

- Verify a running BlueStacks instance with Clash of Clans before entering the main loop
- Use template matching to find wall instances and key UI buttons
- Wall upgrade checks are only allowed after a completed battle and return-home transition
- Wall upgrades require high resources (configured in `config.yaml`; currently gold OR elixir >= 10M)
- Navigate through Attack -> Find a Match
- While searching, keep skipping bases until both gold and elixir are above 1M
- Once a valid base is found, deploy a full preloaded army:
  - 13 dragons
  - 16 balloons
  - all available heroes
- Wait until the Return Home button appears
- Return home and repeat the full loop

# Architecture

- BlueStacks is accessed via ADB on port 5555
- Screen capture is pulled via ADB, CV uses `opencv-python`, and text extraction uses `easyocr`
- Matching is template-first (`template_matcher.py`); no YOLO dependency in the current runtime path
- All ADB actions live in `adb_controller.py` — nothing else calls `subprocess` directly
- The state machine in `state_machine.py` coordinates all logic

# Code Conventions

- No hardcoded coordinates — all come from `config.yaml`
- Functions should be pure where possible; side effects only in controller layer
